# Python 3.12 warns on every `os.fork()` from a multi-threaded process. Every
# fork here is deliberate -- the confinement path exists to fork -- and all of
# them are serialized through `_FORK_LOCK` for exactly the reason the warning
# names. Left on, it puts a two-line DeprecationWarning in the journal for each
# `exec` request, which is noise the host has to filter and a user has to ignore.
